The simulation integrates sub-stepped Newtonian physics where balls experience downward gravity, atmospheric drag, and pair-wise elastic collision responses, while impacts against the spinning hexagon calculate relative contact velocities—including tangential linear velocity imparted by the boundary's rotation—to realistically reflect and transfer momentum.
